WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.820
SpaceX's $295 million megapack order shows Tesla energy scaling into AI data centers as a distinct revenue stream. This is Tesla Shorts Time, Episode 563. SpaceX purchased $295 million worth of Tesla megapacks during the second quarter. The units are expected to support power needs at XAI facilities. The order demonstrates external demand from megapacks from companies building large AI

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:38.260
compute clusters. Energy margins are already higher than automotive and multi-year power purchase agreements add revenue visibility.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:52.640
Future quarterly purchases will indicate whether this customer segment becomes a steady contributor. While energy storage is becoming a standalone platform, Tesla is also building recurring revenue inside the vehicle through software.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:01:04.760
The $99 monthly full self-driving subscription is tracking toward $1.8 million in annual revenue. The figure assumes continued adoption growth from the current base.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:17.840
It represents a shift toward recurring high margin income that does not require additional vehicle production. Current 15% full self-driving subscription adoption serves as an early proof point.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:27.600
Next earnings will show whether uptake accelerates or plateaus. Analysts are already modeling how this software shift could reshape Tesla's valuation.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:46.260
Bank of America kept its $460 price target after trimming 2026 earnings estimates by 17%. The firm argues markets are over-focused on near-term margin pressure and AI spending while underweighting recurring software revenue from full self-driving,

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:56.920
robotaxi, and optimus. It cites the 15% full self-driving subscription adoption rate and expanding robotaxi operations as early proof points.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:10.140
The pivot from one-time vehicle sales to high margin autonomy and robotics is the core thesis. Investors will watch subscription growth and first commercial robotaxi deployments for confirmation.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:21.660
That long-term autonomy bet is playing out against mixed near-term vehicle results. Tesla remained the top imported car brand in South Korea for the sixth consecutive month.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:32.560
The model Y surpassed the Hyundai Grandier to become South Korea's best-selling single vehicle model in July. It also exceeded 10,000 units sold for the fifth straight month.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:47.240
The streak shows sustained demand even as local EV incentives evolve. Sustained volume will test Shanghai production allocation. Strong demand in established markets contrasts with slower progress in newer ones.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:58.180
Customers in India can now book model Y test drives ahead of expected deliveries. The program lets buyers experience performance and features on local roads.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:09.040
It marks a concrete step in Tesla's long planned entry into the Indian market. Delivery volume and service center rollout will determine how quickly the brand scales there.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:20.520
While Tesla works on new markets, it is also expanding where drivers can charge. EV go fast chargers that are still under construction will now show in Tesla's in-car navigation.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:28.460
The change gives drivers visibility into upcoming sites and helps plan longer trips around the expanding third-party network.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:43.120
It also marks further integration of non-Tesla chargers into the Tesla ecosystem. Utilization data from these new locations will reveal whether open access superchargers and partner sites can sustain high uptime.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:55.620
On the regulatory side, one incident is testing how Tesla handles performance modes. A plaintiff claims a dealership handed over a vehicle in insane mode that then crashed during a test drive.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:08.880
The suit alleges inadequate safeguards around performance mode access for new drivers. Tesla will need to show whether existing checkout procedures and mode warnings are sufficient to prevent similar incidents.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:22.320
Court filings will reveal how the company plans to defend the case. Megapack purchases by external AI operators create a demand signal that is independent of Tesla's own vehicle or solar growth.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:35.060
When SpaceX alone commits nearly $300 million in a single quarter, the order book reflects real third-party willingness to pay for grid scale storage rather than internal transfer pricing.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:44.380
This matters because energy margins are already higher than automotive, and each new customer class reduces reliance on any single end market.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:54.700
The same dynamic appears in the Spanish and Arizona PPAs, where Tesla is locking in long-term clean power supply for its own operations or resale.

00:04:54.700 --> 00:05:04.380
These contracts function like forward sales of electricity and storage capacity, converting what used to be a cost center into a contracted revenue stream.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:17.980
Over time, the energy business therefore shifts from an accessory that supports vehicle margins to a standalone platform whose unit economics are driven by power purchase duration and storage utilization rates.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:25.300
The open variable is whether Tesla can maintain installation and commissioning speed as project volume rises.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:34.260
Watch the next few quarterly energy deployments for evidence that external Megapack and PPA activity is becoming a durable second engine.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:43.980
Luxury electric car sales rose 59% year over year in July. BMW held the top spot while Tesla moved into third place.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:50.040
The result reflects broader luxury EV demand rather than Tesla specific incentives.

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:57.160
Monthly share shifts will show whether Tesla can sustain the climb as more competitors launch refreshed models.

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:03.860
The six seat model YL variant previously sold only in China has arrived in the United States.

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:08.960
The configuration adds a third row bench while keeping the same overall footprint.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:15.560
Early customer reactions will show whether the layout appeals to larger families in the American market.

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:21.140
Order data over the next quarter will reveal if the variant gains meaningful share.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:28.640
Tesla signed a 57 megawatt AC power purchase agreement with Zellestra for solar output in Spain.

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:34.280
The deal supplies clean power directly to Tesla operations or customers in the region.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:39.280
It expands Tesla's European energy footprint beyond vehicle sales.

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:46.720
Future PPAs will indicate how quickly the energy business can lock in long-term revenue outside North America.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:52.580
Contour Global signed a PPA with Tesla for a hybrid solar project in Arizona.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:57.320
The agreement adds utility scale solar capacity paired with storage.

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:02.640
It supports Tesla's growing need for reliable clean power near its operations.

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:10.820
Additional Southwest PPAs will reveal how quickly energy procurement is scaling to match AI and manufacturing loads.

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:16.120
Elon Musk linked Optimus deployment to rising Starlink bandwidth demand.

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:20.540
Musk noted robots will consume far more data than current users.

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:26.660
The comment frames Optimus as both a hardware product and a driver of satellite network growth.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:32.440
It also suggests internal Tesla use of Optimus could accelerate Starlink adoption.

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:36.860
Production timelines for both programs will show whether the linkage holds.

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:41.740
Morningstar labeled Tesla shares very attractive after recent earnings.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:48.540
The research firm highlighted the valuation reset as an entry point despite near-term earnings pressure.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:55.720
The note focuses on long-term optionality in autonomy and robotics rather than current vehicle margins.

00:07:55.720 --> 00:08:02.120
It joins other analyst commentaries suggesting the post earnings dip created a buying opportunity.

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:07.780
Price action over the next several sessions will test whether that view gains broader traction.

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:13.120
Use Tesla prices lead a broader rebound in the EV resale market.

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:19.060
Data shows Tesla models posting the strongest recovery among electric vehicles in recent weeks.

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:24.660
The rebound follows earlier depreciation that had concerns some owners and lenders.

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:33.160
Stronger resale values could ease financing terms for new buyers and support residual value assumptions in Tesla's leasing programs.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:38.360
Monthly used price indices will confirm whether the trend holds through the summer.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:42.880
A cyber cab was spotted during testing near the Las Vegas strip.

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:53.040
Owners and bystanders captured photos of the vehicle undergoing real-world evaluation near Park MGM with two testers confirming active development work.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:59.920
Sightings like this give the first public glimpses of how the Robotaxi looks and behaves in everyday traffic.

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:05.300
More frequent reports from multiple cities would indicate broader testing is underway.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:11.060
SpaceX and NVIDIA partnered on Orbital AI hardware for StarMine satellites.

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:18.720
The collaboration brings NVIDIA Ruben GPUs into SpaceX satellite designs aimed at AI workloads.

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:23.900
Musk confirmed an exclusive NVIDIA hardware commitment following the announcement.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:31.900
The move ties Tesla adjacent AI ambitions to Orbital infrastructure in a way that goes beyond ground-based dojo clusters.

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:38.980
Deployment timelines will show whether satellite-based inference becomes a meaningful complement to terrestrial compute.

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:45.400
Zellestra commissioned three Spanish solar plants under the 57 megawatt Tesla PPA.

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:50.440
The projects have reached commercial operation and are now feeding power into the grid.

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:55.260
The commissioning marks the first visible output from the recently signed agreement.

00:09:56.060 --> 00:10:02.720
It demonstrates how quickly utility scale solar paired with Tesla storage can move from contract to generation.

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:08.640
Additional plant completions will clarify the pace of Tesla's European energy rollout.

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:16.620
Before we go, keep an eye on how quickly the Indian Test Drive program converts into actual deliveries and service center openings.

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:19.640
And that's a wrap on today's Tesla news.

